# deploy/requirements-tools.in - input for requirements-tools.lock: the Python recon
# tools the active-scanner image runs, kept in their OWN virtualenv (/opt/venv-tools)
# so their dependency trees can never conflict with SpiderFoot's application venv.
#
# Dropped from the old list, deliberately (see deploy/README.md "Active-scanner tools"):
#   trufflehog - PyPI's `trufflehog` is the abandoned 2021 v2.1.13; the maintained v3 is
#                a Go binary, installed from a checksummed release instead.
#   linkfinder - no release in 2.5 years; katana (-jc) does JavaScript endpoint discovery.
dnstwist
snallygaster
wafw00f
arjun
sslyze
#
# Identity tools, added 2026-11-14 (modules sfp_tool_maigret and sfp_tool_user_scanner). Pinned exactly: both are fast-moving
# projects (user-scanner released every one to two weeks), so a newer version is taken deliberately, not by a rebuild.
#   maigret      - username search on ~5,900 sites (MIT; run with --no-autoupdate --no-recursion, never --ai).
#   user-scanner - which sites an email address is registered on (MIT; its update check and prompts are switched off by the module).
# The newest version at least 14 days old: user-scanner 1.5.2.5 was released 2026-11-03.
maigret==0.6.6
user-scanner==1.5.2.3
